.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.decrypted.json

# The published payload lives on its own branch, force-pushed to a single commit each
# time. It is written here by the pipeline and by local test builds, and committing it
# to `main` would put an incompressible 436 KB blob into the history of the code.
data/portfolio.enc

# The browser harness pulls in ~100 packages and a 130 MB Chromium. Both are rebuilt
# from `package-lock.json` on every run, here and on the runner.
.github/checks/node_modules/
# Written by `build_fixture_payload.py --plaintext` when someone wants to read the
# synthetic payload. It is invented data and harmless, but there is no reason for a
# generated file to be committed beside the generator that makes it.
.github/checks/fixtures/*.json

# Python leaves these beside the fixture generator, and a .pyc embeds the absolute
# path it was compiled from — on this machine that is the owner's Windows user
# directory. In a public repository that is a small, permanent leak for no benefit.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
